      "title": "PDO Professional Development Coordinator (SCUPA/GFPC 1)",
      "description": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | PDO Professional Development Coordinator (SCUPA/GFPC 1) Skip to Main Content About Academics Administrative Offices Admissions Athletics News and Events myShip Employment Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Useful Links Human Resources Social Equity Benefits Campus Safety & Security PDO Professional Development Coordinator (SCUPA/GFPC 1) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration candidates should apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu until the position is filled with acceptance of materials. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regards to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Posting Details Position Information Working Title PDO Professional Development Coordinator (SCUPA/GFPC 1) Department Teacher Education Position Category Support Staff Posting Number SP00873 Position End Date (if other than Permanent) 08/05/2028 Hours per Week 37.5 Salary Range The anticipated salary will be $48,411 (as of 8/22/2026) annually annually including extensive benefits package. Full/Part Time Full Time Type of Position Permanent Position Summary Information General Description/Position Purpose Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at Shippensburg University , located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees! Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage. Choose from two generous retirement plans: Alternative Retirement Plan ( ARP ): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting. State Employees’ Retirement System ( SERS ): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement. Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more! See full details in link below. Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) The Outreach Coordinator position’s primary purpose is to increase early childhood educators’ understanding about what the PDO is and how their career pathways in ECE can expand and advance with PDO -sponsored tuition and other supports. The overarching PDO goal is to increase the credentials and professional regard of all Pennsylvania EC educators as we build a pipeline of qualified people in this workforce-critical sector. This is a grant funded program position for 2 years Summary of Duties Manage participant eligibility, enrollment, and ongoing compliance by collecting and verifying required employment, wage, residency, academic, and program documentation. Confirm and accurately record participant eligibility through the PD Registry and related online systems. Ensure all required enrollment documents, including Commitment Forms and FERPA releases, are complete and properly submitted. Support the planning and coordination of professional development events, including scheduling, registration, participant communication, meeting locations, trainer logistics, travel arrangements, and materials. Guide Professional Development Organization and grant-funded students through the full Child Development Associate credentialing process. Provide individualized advising, coaching, and mentoring related to CDA requirements, competency standards, portfolios, documentation, assessments, and professional writing. Review candidate portfolios and supporting documentation for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with CDA Council guidelines. Monitor student progress, maintain detailed records, and support timely completion of all credentialing requirements. Facilitate workshops and one-on-one support sessions to strengthen reflective practice, accountability, confidence, and professional growth. Prepare candidates for CDA verification visits and competency-based assessments. Collaborate with instructors, administrators, and field supervisors to support candidate success. Remain current on CDA Council policies, credentialing requirements, and early childhood education best practices. Provide professional development coordination and CDA guidance to School to Work Round 6 Grant and OCDEL PDO students. Full job description will be provided at time of interview. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in early childhood education, Education, or related field required. Preferred Qualifications Relevant experience in early childhood professional development, student advising, program coordinator, Child Development Associate ( CDA ) preferred. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary For full consideration candidates should apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu until the position is filled with acceptance of materials. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regards to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Additional Information Shippensburg University employees value teamwork and collaboration, are dependable, take initiative, solve problems effectively, communicate clearly and support organizational change. University employees must possess good interpersonal skills and be able to communicate effectively with all members of the campus community. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently an employee at Shippensburg University? Yes No * Are you currently covered by the SCUPA collective bargaining agreement? yes no * Do you possess a Bachelor's degree in Early Childhood Education or related field? Yes No * Do you have experience working in early childhood professional development, student advising, or program coordinating? Yes No * Do you have Child Development Associate (CDA) credentials? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Employer website Indeed CareerLink HigherEd Jobs LinkedIn Advertisement /Publication Personal Referral * What interests you about working at Shippensburg University? Benefits Salary Tuition Waiver Working in Higher Education Closer To Home Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts 1 List of References Optional Documents This page is an official publication of Shippensburg University: A member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education . Shippensburg University - 1871 Old Main Drive - Shippensburg, PA 17257 - (717) 477-7447 Ask a Question/Provide Feedback | Privacy Statement | View on Mobile To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
