      "title": "Director of First Generation Student Success GFPC 2",
      "description": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | Director of First Generation Student Success GFPC 2 Skip to Main Content About Academics Administrative Offices Admissions Athletics News and Events myShip Employment Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Useful Links Human Resources Social Equity Benefits Campus Safety & Security Director of First Generation Student Success GFPC 2 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration, all candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials continuing until the posting is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regards to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Posting Details Position Information Working Title Director of First Generation Student Success GFPC 2 Department Student Retention Initiative Position Category Support Staff Posting Number SP00884 Position End Date (if other than Permanent) 09/30/2031 Hours per Week 37.5 Salary Range The anticipated salary will be $56,079 annually and includes an extensive benefits package and tuition waiver for the employee and dependents. Full/Part Time Full Time Type of Position Temporary Position Summary Information General Description/Position Purpose Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at Shippensburg University , located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees! Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage. Choose from two generous retirement plans: Alternative Retirement Plan ( ARP ): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting. State Employees’ Retirement System ( SERS ): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement. Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more! See full details in link below Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) This grant-funded position is anticipated to continue through September 30, 2031. This position will required to work some weekends and evenings for specialized programs The Director of First Generation Student Success is responsible for supporting first-generation students at Shippensburg University and increasing their retention and graduation rates, with special emphasis on first-generation students who are Pell Grant recipients. Using a case-management approach through Navigate360, the Director will support students from recruitment and onboarding through degree completion by managing Early Alerts, conducting proactive outreach, monitoring attendance and academic progress, and connecting students with appropriate resources. The Director will lead Tri-Alpha Honor Society initiatives, coordinate First-Generation Student Celebration Day, develop a layered mentoring network, support family engagement, and collaborate with the Career Center on networking, alumni engagement, and experiential learning opportunities. Additional responsibilities include supporting retention strategies, assessing academic, financial, and personal wellness, providing financial literacy and wellness programming, creating engagement opportunities focused on first-generation experiences and belonging, establishing a designated space for first-generation students, tracking participation and student outcomes, providing regular reports and assessment data, and supervising a graduate assistant. Other duties may be assigned as needed. A full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview. Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree required from a regionally accredited institution; 2-3 years of experience working in higher education working directly with students Ability to take initiative and plan, organize, coordinate, and perform work in complex situations where competing priorities exist. Effective interpersonal, problem solving and communication skills Demonstrated experience in building positive working relationships with campus constituents Commitment to an inclusive and diverse campus environment Preferred Qualifications 5 years of experience working as a student success coach or other student success related position in higher education Experience working with Navigate360 or a comparable student success platform Experience supervising graduate and undergraduate students Experience with federally funded grants and data reporting Breadth of knowledge about first-generation college students including promising, effective, and best practices. Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary For full consideration, all candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials continuing until the posting is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regards to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Additional Information All Shippensburg University employees are expected to demonstrate an understanding of and commitment to the University’s core values of teamwork and collaboration, dependability, initiative, problem solving, and clear communication. University employees are expected to demonstrate good interpersonal and communication skills with all members of the campus community. They will strive to maintain integrity, effectiveness and efficiency by upholding customer service throughout all levels of performance. All university employees are required to comply with university policies, state and federal laws/statutes prohibiting any type of Discrimination, Harassment or Retaliation. Safeguarding confidential, personal data and/or records of employees, students, customers and other related constituents is the responsibility of all University employees. It is the duty of all members of the University community to take part in the maintenance of a safe campus. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently covered by the SCUPA collective bargaining agreement? yes no * Are you a current employee of Shippensburg University? Yes No * What interests you about working at Shippensburg University? Benefits Salary Tuition Waiver Working in Higher Education Closer To Home * Do you have a Master’s Degree required from a regionally accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have 2-3 years of experience working in higher education working directly with students? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Employer website Indeed CareerLink HigherEd Jobs LinkedIn Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts 1 List of References Optional Documents This page is an official publication of Shippensburg University: A member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education . Shippensburg University - 1871 Old Main Drive - Shippensburg, PA 17257 - (717) 477-7447 Ask a Question/Provide Feedback | Privacy Statement | View on Mobile To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3562": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | Police Officer Skip to Main Content About Academics Administrative Offices Admissions Athletics News and Events myShip Employment Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Useful Links Human Resources Social Equity Benefits Campus Safety & Security Police Officer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration all candidates should apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials until the search has been closed. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Posting Details Position Information Working Title Police Officer Department Public Safety Position Category Support Staff Posting Number SP00845 Position End Date (if other than Permanent) Hours per Week 40 Salary Range Annual Salary is $52, 014 plus comprehensive benefits including tuition waivers for employee and dependents. Full/Part Time Full Time Type of Position Permanent Position Summary Information General Description/Position Purpose Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at Shippensburg University , located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees! Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage. Choose from two generous retirement plans: Alternative Retirement Plan ( ARP ): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting. State Employees’ Retirement System ( SERS ): employee may choose between SERS Class A3 with 6.25% employee contribution or SERS Class A4 with 9.3% employee contribution, with a 10-year vesting requirement. 100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period! Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more! See full details in link below (for PASSHE Benefits) Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) Shippensburg University is currently accepting applications for the position of Police Officer. This position will work a permanent shift. To enforce applicable policies and laws in university buildings and grounds. To protect the property of the Commonwealth in all buildings and grounds of the University and to exclude disorderly persons from same. To exercise powers of arrest under authority of law or ordinance wherein the University is located. To perform traffic and crowd control duties while enforcing all traffic laws and regulations of the Commonwealth and the University. Investigate traffic accidents, prepare accident reports and follow-up procedures as may be necessary. To investigate all crimes. To render assistance to those in distress. To provide public service to both residents and visitors to the University. To provide emergency services as may be necessary and/or directed by standing procedures for all types of disorder or disasters. To patrol and secure buildings and grounds as may be necessary during the tour of duty. To operate the University Communications System in accordance with existing FCC rules and regulations. To be responsible for the safety, control and use of Commonwealth property assigned to the University Police Department or the University. To cooperate with all other law enforcement agencies requesting assistance and/or information. To assume the duties of acting supervisor in their absence. Possession of basic computer skills necessary to complete reports and enter information into the department Informant system. Minimum Qualifications Must have completed the requirements of Act 120. Possession of the Act 120 certification is required. Must meet the requirements of the department’s firearms qualification process. Must have or be able to obtain a valid PA driver’s license. Must meet the qualifications regarding strength, agility and health. Should have one year of police experience or any equivalent experience or training. An associate’s degree with major course work in police science, police administration or a closely related field may be substituted for one year of police experience. Preferred Qualifications Posting Detail Information Open Date 03/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary For full consideration all candidates should apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials until the search has been closed. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Additional Information All Shippensburg University employees are expected to demonstrate an understanding of and commitment to the University’s core values of teamwork and collaboration, dependability, initiative, problem solving, and clear communication. University employees are expected to demonstrate good interpersonal and communication skills with all members of the campus community. They will strive to maintain integrity, effectiveness and efficiency by upholding customer service throughout all levels of performance. All university employees are required to comply with university policies, state and federal laws/statutes prohibiting any type of Discrimination, Harassment or Retaliation. Safeguarding confidential, personal data and/or records of employees, students, customers and other related constituents is the responsibility of all University employees. It is the duty of all members of the University community to take part in the maintenance of a safe campus. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently possess Act 120 certification? yes no * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Employer website Indeed CareerLink HigherEd Job LinkedIn Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral * What interests you about working at Shippensburg University? Benefits Salary Tuition Waiver Working in Higher Education Closer to Home Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application List of References Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts 1 This page is an official publication of Shippensburg University: A member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education . Shippensburg University - 1871 Old Main Drive - Shippensburg, PA 17257 - (717) 477-7447 Ask a Question/Provide Feedback | Privacy Statement | View on Mobile To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
