    "https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3559": {
      "title": "Payroll Manager",
      "description": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | Payroll Manager Skip to Main Content About Academics Administrative Offices Admissions Athletics News and Events myShip Employment Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Useful Links Human Resources Social Equity Benefits Campus Safety & Security Payroll Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration, all candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials continuing until the posting is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Posting Details Position Information Working Title Payroll Manager Department Administration and Finance Position Category Administration/Management Posting Number SP00887 Position End Date (if other than Permanent) Hours per Week 37.5 hours per week. This position is scheduled to work Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Salary Range Salary Range: $67,500–$85,000 annually, based on experience, plus a comprehensive benefits package. Full/Part Time Full Time Type of Position Permanent Position Summary Information General Description/Position Purpose Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at Shippensburg University , located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduate, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words. We are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success. Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees! Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage . Choose from two generous retirement plans : Alternative Retirement Plan ( ARP ):5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting State Employees’ Retirement System ( SERS ): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement 100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period! Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more! See full details in link below (for PASSHE Benefits) Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) General Position Description Shippensburg University is seeking a knowledgeable, resourceful, and detail-oriented Payroll Manager to oversee the University’s payroll operations. This key position within Human Resources requires a proactive, solutions-oriented professional who demonstrates independent judgment, resourcefulness, accountability, and a commitment to operational excellence. The successful candidate will play a critical role in ensuring the accurate, timely, and compliant processing of University payroll while promoting operational efficiency, continuous process improvement, and exceptional customer service. Summary of Responsibilities Oversee biweekly payroll operations for faculty, staff, and student employees, ensuring accurate, timely, and compliant payroll processing. Administer complex payroll transactions, including overtime, shift differentials, faculty overload, supplemental compensation, deductions, payroll adjustments, and leave payouts. Research, interpret, and apply collective bargaining agreements, University and PASSHE policies, and applicable regulations. Conduct payroll audits, reconcile discrepancies, implement timely corrective actions, and maintain effective internal controls. Independently research, investigate, and resolve complex payroll issues, demonstrating sound judgment, accountability, and a proactive approach to problem-solving. Maintain accurate payroll and leave records, ensure data integrity within SAP and related systems, prepare reports, and identify opportunities for process improvement. Collaborate with University departments and PASSHE partners, providing timely communication, guidance, follow-through, and appropriate escalation of payroll matters. Provide oversight and guidance for student payroll functions. A full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, Human Resources, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible payroll experience, preferably in a complex organizational environment. Thorough knowledge of federal, state, and local payroll laws, wage and hour regulations, tax requirements, and payroll compliance standards. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply collective bargaining agreements, organizational policies, and applicable regulations. Experience with payroll processing, auditing, reconciliation, and maintaining accurate payroll records. Proficiency with computerized payroll systems, Microsoft Excel, and payroll reporting tools. Strong analytical, critical-thinking, and problem-solving skills, with demonstrated resourcefulness and the ability to independently research and resolve complex issues. Exceptional attention to detail, organizational skills, and the ability to manage competing priorities and meet strict deadlines. Demonstrated initiative, accountability, sound judgment, and commitment to confidentiality and accuracy. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a collaborative, customer-focused approach. Demonstrated ability to provide leadership, guidance, and oversight of payroll operations, fostering accountability, accuracy, and continuous improvement. Preferred Qualifications Payroll experience in higher education or the public sector. Experience administering payroll in a unionized environment with multiple collective bargaining agreements. Experience utilizing SAP for payroll processing, reporting, and auditing. Experience administering complex compensation arrangements, including faculty overload, supplemental compensation, and leave payouts. Experience supervising or providing functional oversight to payroll staff. Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary For full consideration, all candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials continuing until the posting is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Additional Information All Shippensburg University employees are expected to demonstrate an understanding of and commitment to the University’s core values of teamwork and collaboration, dependability, initiative, problem-solving, and clear communication. University employees are expected to demonstrate good interpersonal and communication skills with all members of the campus community. They will strive to maintain integrity, effectiveness, and efficiency by upholding customer service throughout all levels of performance. All university employees are required to comply with university policies, state and federal laws/statutes prohibiting any type of Discrimination, Harassment or Retaliation. Safeguarding confidential, personal data and/or records of employees, students, customers and other related constituents is the responsibility of all University employees. It is the duty of all members of the University community to take part in the maintenance of a safe campus. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess a bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, business administration, human resources, related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience? YES NO * Do you have a minimum of five years of experience in Payroll? YES NO * Do you have experience working in a unionized environment? YES NO * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Employer website Indeed CareerLink HigherEd Job LinkedIn Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral * What interests you about working at Shippensburg University? Benefits Salary Tuition Waiver Working in Higher Education Closer to home Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts 1 List of References Optional Documents This page is an official publication of Shippensburg University: A member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education . Shippensburg University - 1871 Old Main Drive - Shippensburg, PA 17257 - (717) 477-7447 Ask a Question/Provide Feedback | Privacy Statement | View on Mobile To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3561": {
      "title": "Student Teaching Supervisor",
      "description": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | Student Teaching Supervisor Skip to Main Content About Academics Administrative Offices Admissions Athletics News and Events myShip Employment Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Useful Links Human Resources Social Equity Benefits Campus Safety & Security Student Teaching Supervisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application procedure: All candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with review of applications beginning immediately and continuing until the position is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. For an application to be considered complete, candidates must submit a letter of application, curriculum vita, unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts (official transcripts required if granted an on-campus interview), and three letters of recommendation from teacher education professionals (principals, professors, teachers, professional educators, higher education administrators). Copies of any professional certificates may also be submitted (optional). Incomplete applications will not be considered. Posting Details Position Information Working Title Student Teaching Supervisor Department Teacher Education Position Category Adjunct Faculty Track Temporary Rank Instructor Percentage of Time Other If other, please indicate Term Spring 2027 Posting Number FP00256 Position Start Date Position End Date (if other than Permanent) Salary / Wage Range Quick Link https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3428 Position Summary Information General Description/Position Purpose The Department of Teacher Education seeks instructors to supervise student teachers. Selected candidates will be added to a team of university supervisors who will be used on an as-needed basis during the fall and spring semesters. As a university supervisor, you will oversee the student teaching experience for assigned students. Primary duties include mentoring, instructional coaching, and collaborating with host teachers. Responsibilities also encompass the writing of evaluations and recommendation letters, responding to emails and phone calls in a timely manner, and the completion of professorial duties. The work requires travel to local schools and the occasional need to attend campus meetings/events. Please see course catalog for course description ( ECED 489)- https://catalog.ship.edu/index.php Minimum Qualifications A master’s degree in the field of education, with at least 5 years experience teaching in K-8 is required. Applicants who meet the minimum requirements will be certified to be placed in our part-time adjunct faculty pool and will remain in the pool while the pool is active. As need arises, applicants in the pool will be considered and contacted for an on-campus interview. As part of a successful on-campus interview process, candidates will be expected to provide a demonstration of teaching effectiveness and evidence of understanding diverse populations. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate and at least one year of college-level teaching experience or equivalent, experience working with diverse learners is preferred. Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Application procedure: All candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with review of applications beginning immediately and continuing until the position is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper applications will not be considered. For an application to be considered complete, candidates must submit a letter of application, curriculum vita, unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts (official transcripts required if granted an on-campus interview), and three letters of recommendation from teacher education professionals (principals, professors, teachers, professional educators, higher education administrators). Copies of any professional certificates may also be submitted (optional). Incomplete applications will not be considered. Additional Information Offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check as well as sufficient course enrollment and budget allocations. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is an equal opportunity employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. All university employees are required to comply with university policies, state and federal laws/statutes prohibiting any type of Discrimination, Harassment, or Retaliation. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 List of References Other Document Other Document 2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). This page is an official publication of Shippensburg University: A member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education . Shippensburg University - 1871 Old Main Drive - Shippensburg, PA 17257 - (717) 477-7447 Ask a Question/Provide Feedback | Privacy Statement | View on Mobile To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
